  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Strong Goldbach Conjecture}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Conjecture:\nthen:\n. forAll: n is \\integer\n  where:\n  . \\integer.two \\:integer.less?:/ n\n  . n is? \\(even)::integer\n  then:\n  . exists: p, q is \\integer\n    suchThat:\n    . p is? \\(prime)::integer\n    . q is? \\(prime)::integer\n    . n = p \\.integer.+./ q\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Strong Goldbach Conjecture\"\n. description: \"Every even integer greater than two is the sum of two primes;\n                the two primes are not required to be distinct.\"\nId: \"1945a57b-f397-4f58-b515-fd8878910f2e\"",
